{"id":"666393432","kind":"article","title":"可探索媒介中的有限性假设","author":"Issa Rice","original_authors":["Issa Rice"],"original_source_urls":["https://wiki.issarice.com/wiki/Finiteness_assumption_in_explorable_media"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"Issawiki & Learning","date":"2023-11-12","updated":"2026-10-27","votes":8,"comment_count":0,"minutes":2,"chars":748,"keywords":["可探索媒介","数学教育","无穷对象","交互式学习","证明生成"],"summary":"作者认为电子游戏等可探索媒介通常假设对象有限且离散，因此难以呈现数学证明中的无穷对象、任意对象和不可能的反例。以《The Witness》的谜题为例，他指出游戏谜题虽可逐步组合仍受有限状态限制，并追问如何设计能支持一般数学推理的交互媒介。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/666393432","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":3,"title":"参见"},{"id":"sec-2","level":3,"title":"链接到本文"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"wEVF0gyC\"><b>电子游戏里的对象都是离散且有限的</b>。可探索和交互式媒体（尤其是<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/wiki/Explorable_explanation\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">可探索的解释</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup>）似乎经过有限性假设的烘焙，这使得处理数学中的「无限」或「任意」时都显得棘手。「无限」的一个典例是「设 <img alt=\"x\" class=\"math-eq\" eeimg=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://www.zhihu.com/equation?tex=x\"/> 是 <img alt=\"X\" class=\"math-eq\" eeimg=\"1\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://www.zhihu.com/equation?tex=X\"/> 的任意元素」，你在做数学证明时经常遇到，其中 X 是讨论的某类对象。游戏中「移动」时，没什么简单直接的办法，可以搞成这样。</p><p data-pid=\"0UGc9Vxw\">例子：</p><ul><li data-pid=\"15Q0l8Q9\"> 可探索的媒介  <a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.comhttps//explorabl.es/math/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://explorabl.es/math/</a><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"Kf-QC0cT\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL5dr1EHvfwpNYbS_yqCZg30lEnpiEF6O2\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">见证者</a>中从简单的谜题开始构建复杂的谜题。但是每个谜题都是有限的（有限的棋盘尺寸，有限的状态空间)<br/> </li></ul><p data-pid=\"M5u4n3tC\">我感兴趣的那种可探索的媒介, 会以某种方式对 证明编写/ 证明生成 过程进行编码，以便用户可以进行真正的数学运算。但是你如何证明关于「任意紧凑的度量空间」这种东西的命题？你将如何 “探索” 依赖反证法的命题（这需要呈现「不可能的反例」）？</p><p data-pid=\"tJA2TkD8\">数学的棘手之处在于您经常需要处理「无穷」，就是说, 那些不能在有限情况下表示的对象（例如数列）你得清楚地比划出来。我认为，你可以退回到<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/wiki/Probability_and_statistics_as_fields_with_an_exploratory_medium\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">组合学</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup>等领域去处理有限对象，但提出适用于任何领域的通用解决方案，更会令哥哥满意。</p><h3 id=\"sec-1\">参见</h3><ul><li data-pid=\"_Pxsa13z\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/wiki/Video_games_comparison_to_math\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">游戏 vs 数学</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"5R6ubc9S\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/wiki/Probability_and_statistics_as_fields_with_an_exploratory_medium\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">概率和统计是具有可探索媒介的领域</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"K42s9Pr7\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/wiki/Representing_impossibilities\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">表示不可能的情况</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup><br/> </li></ul><h3 id=\"sec-2\">链接到本文</h3><ul><li data-pid=\"KsgoNxmi\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/wiki/Explorable_explanation\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">可探索的解释</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup> ‎ (<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/index.php?title=Special:WhatLinksHere&amp;target=Explorable+explanation\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">← links</a>)<br/> </li><li data-pid=\"vjzzwDZx\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/index.php?title=Video_games_work_with_finite_and_discrete_objects&amp;redirect=no\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">电子游戏使用有限且离散对象</a> (redirect page) ‎ (<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/index.php?title=Special:WhatLinksHere&amp;target=Video+games+work+with+finite+and+discrete+objects\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">← links</a>)<br/> </li><ul><li data-pid=\"pnxtbjyK\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/wiki/Video_games_comparison_to_math\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">对比数学与电子游戏</a> ‎ (<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/index.php?title=Special:WhatLinksHere&amp;target=Video+games+comparison+to+math\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">← links</a>)<br/> </li></ul><li data-pid=\"au4FsiIe\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/wiki/Representing_impossibilities\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">表示不可能的情况</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup> ‎ (<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/index.php?title=Special:WhatLinksHere&amp;target=Representing+impossibilities\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">← links</a>)<br/> </li></ul><p class=\"ztext-empty-paragraph\"><br/></p><blockquote data-pid=\"ng41Pf9b\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"http://paratranz.cn/projects/3131\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Thoughts Memo</a> 汉化组译制<br/>感谢主要译者 <span class=\"nolink\">偶然奇怪~ ☆</span>、校对 Jarrett Ye<br/>原文：<a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://wiki.issarice.com/wiki/Finiteness_assumption_in_explorable_media\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Finiteness assumption in explorable media</a></blockquote><hr/><ol class=\"references\"><li id=\"ref-1\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-1\">↩</a> 可探索的解释 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"598332415\" href=\"#/post/598332415\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-2\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-2\">↩</a> 概率和统计是具有可探索媒介的领域 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"618757945\" href=\"#/post/618757945\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-3\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-3\">↩</a> 对比数学与电子游戏 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"716414197\" href=\"#/post/716414197\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li><li id=\"ref-4\"><a aria-label=\"返回正文\" class=\"ref-back\" href=\"#cite-4\">↩</a> 表示不可能的情况 <a class=\"tm-internal\" data-tm-id=\"592187312\" href=\"#/post/592187312\">站内阅读 ↗</a></li></ol>","rec_chain":[{"id":"660401630","title":"卡片分享能让你有理由制作价值稍低的卡片","author":"Issa Rice","votes":5,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏上一篇 · Issawiki & Learning"},{"id":"691811637","title":"数学中的沉默宣言会是什么样的？","author":"Issa Rice","votes":13,"minutes":1,"reason":"同专栏下一篇 · Issawiki & Learning"},{"id":"598332415","title":"可探索的解释","author":"Issa Rice","votes":6,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"716414197","title":"对比数学与电子游戏","author":"Issa Rice","votes":16,"minutes":1,"reason":"本文直接引用"},{"id":"618757945","title":"概率和统计是具有可探索媒介的领域","author":"Issa Rice","votes":6,"minutes":2,"reason":"本文直接引用"}],"rec_bridge":[{"id":"1944442771533432041","title":"纠错练习","author":"Vipul","votes":8,"minutes":3,"reason":"跨学派视角 · Vipul"}],"rec_answers":[]}